✔ patient DELETE routes delegate one version-guarded tombstone and required audit transaction (120.561973ms)
✔ patient GET and PUT handlers preserve tombstones through the profile port and writer (404 contract) (89.573068ms)
✔ profile tombstone guard rejects broken imports, delegation, filters, 404s and final updates (266.832815ms)
ℹ 20 in-memory rejection cases per route; production files unchanged
✔ the schema owner keeps the additive ensureColumn guards for the tombstone columns (0.252281ms)
✔ primary patient list reads exclude soft-deleted patients (0.259482ms)
✔ ambulatories/clear is membership-based, soft-deletes and stays test-only (0.301125ms)
✔ the membership-clear helper tombstones with the dedicated reason (0.162926ms)
✔ AST guard isolates direct patient-read chains and normalizes their fingerprints (2.602452ms)
✔ AST allowlist consumes fingerprints and rejects stale, substituted, or duplicate reads (0.842663ms)
✔ AST guard follows a local immutable predicate without accepting aliases, mutation, or shadowing (1.941213ms)
✔ AST guard follows AND-only predicate paths and invalidates every query after an unsafe use (14.831428ms)
ℹ 19 rejected AND/escape cases, plus all-use invalidation of two patient queries
✔ patients table access stays behind activePatients() outside the allowlist (856.093797ms)
